<title>GERMANY: Plettac buys Grundig's security unit.</title>
<headline>Plettac buys Grundig's security unit.</headline>
<dateline>PLETTENBERG, Germany 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Plettac AG said on Wednesday it would buy the video and security technology business of Grundig Professional Electronics GmbH.</p>
<p>The two have signed a letter of intent, and the sale should take effect on January 1, 1997. Grundig AG is a unit of Philips Electronics NV.</p>
<p>The Grundig unit has annual sales of 120 million marks and a market share of 20 percent, Plettac said.</p>
<p>Security will become Plettac's third-largest division, with sales of 200 million marks.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
